// Conținut editorial per plajă — traducere ENGLEZĂ (30 din 188, în lucru).
// Aceeași structură ca beach-content-data.js (română), cheile sunt numele
// EXACT din attractions-data.js. Se încarcă DOAR când pagina cere lang=uk,
// nu la fiecare cerere — vezi server.js, unde e cerut condiționat.
module.exports = {
  "Plaja Golden Beach Thassos": {
    scurt: "Golden Beach (or Chrysi Ammoudia) is the longest, most popular and spectacular beach on Thassos. Stretching for several kilometres in a huge bay surrounded by green mountains, it fully lives up to its name thanks to fine sand that glitters like gold under the sun. The water is crystal clear with an extremely gentle entry, making it a dream spot where kids can play safely and adults can relax without a care.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach practically links two important tourist villages, Skala Potamia and Skala Panagia. Local buses exist, but they run on a fixed schedule and get packed in high season. With a rental car you have the freedom to explore both ends of the bay, drop your heavy bags a few steps from your sunbed, and drive up in the evening to the traditional village of Panagia for dinner under the plane trees. Parking is generous along the whole beach, with both free public spots and dedicated beach-bar parking.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "Where the beach meets the rocky edges of the bay, marine life is very active and the water is perfectly clear." }, { titlu: "Kite or sand-game gear", text: "The beach is so wide and open in places that you have plenty of space for relaxed activities without bothering anyone else." }, { titlu: "Water-resistant sunscreen", text: "The sea breeze here is deceptive and it's easy to get sunburnt while walking along the long shoreline." }],
    preturi: "A set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs between €10-15, though most beach bars will give you the sunbeds for free with a minimum drink purchase of the same value (a beer, coffee, or juice). A gyros at the beachfront taverns runs around €4-5, and a full meal for two comes to about €30-40.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A kids' paradise", text: "Parents consistently praise how far out you have to walk before the water reaches your waist." }, { titlu: "A lively beachfront", text: "Tourists appreciate having everything within a minute's walk: supermarkets, showers, a changing cabin, and excellent tavernas." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Head to the left end of the beach (Skala Panagia side) for even finer sand and a completely wave-free sea — the most sheltered corner of the whole bay." }],
  },
  "Plaja Saliara (Marble Beach) Thassos": {
    scurt: "Saliara is arguably the most exotic and unique beach on Thassos. Instead of classic sand, the whole beach is made of small, perfectly rounded white marble pebbles (sourced from the nearby quarry). Because of this white backdrop, the sea takes on such an intense electric turquoise that you'd swear you were in the Caribbean or the Maldives. It's an incredibly photogenic spot, though the pure white glare reflects the sun very strongly.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is isolated and tucked away on the island's north-east coast, and public transport doesn't reach it at all. From the paved main road toward Makryammos, you'll need to cover about 4-5km of unpaved forest track. It's a dusty road, full of bumps and stones, which is why a car is absolutely necessary to get there safely and without rushing. The lower parking area is set right in the pine forest and is free.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Polarised sunglasses", text: "Light reflected off the white marble pebbles is blinding at midday. Without good sunglasses, it's hard to enjoy the view." }, { titlu: "Beach sandals or aqua shoes", text: "The marble pebbles get extremely hot under the blazing sun, and walking barefoot to the water can be a real challenge." }, { titlu: "Underwater camera or waterproof case", text: "Water clarity in this bay is legendary — perfect for underwater filming and photos." }],
    preturi: "The beach is run entirely by one exclusive beach bar, so prices run higher than the island average. Renting a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella starts at €25-35 (depending on the row), and most of the time that price covers access only, not drinks. A coffee or beer at the bar costs around €5-6.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Get ready for dust", text: "Every visitor warns that after the drive in, your car will be covered in a fine layer of white marble dust." }, { titlu: "Very crowded in season", text: "Thanks to its social-media fame, the beach fills up completely from the early morning hours." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive very early, ideally before 08:45. You'll get the best shaded parking spot, a front-row sunbed, and be able to take stunning photos before the bay fills with people." }],
  },
  "Plaja Navagio Zakynthos": {
    scurt: "Navagio Beach (Shipwreck Beach) is, without a doubt, the most famous and photographed beach in all of Greece. Tucked into an isolated bay on the north-west coast, it's surrounded by vertical white limestone cliffs over 200 metres tall. On the fine white-pebble shore rests the wreck of the Panagiotis, which ran aground in 1980. The water colour here is truly surreal — a milky, glowing, neon-intense blue, caused by underwater sulphur springs and dissolved limestone.",
    cumAjungi: "The only way to reach the lower Navagio beach is by sea. Even so, you definitely need a car to reach the ports the speedboats leave from (such as Porto Vromi, Agios Nikolaos, or Skinari). The mountain road to these ports is spectacular, full of hairpin turns and dramatic scenery. On top of that, having a car lets you later drive up to the clifftop viewpoint for the famous overhead photo. Parking at the ports is free, but spots are limited in August.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Sturdy beach sandals or aqua shoes", text: "The beach isn't fine sand but round white pebbles that get very hot in the sun and can be painful to walk on." }, { titlu: "A thin windbreaker jacket", text: "The speedboats taking you into the bay move fast, and you can get quite wet from the spray." }, { titlu: "Hat and sunglasses", text: "The white cliffs reflect sunlight like a giant mirror, and down on the beach there's absolutely no shade or facilities." }],
    preturi: "A speedboat excursion ticket (usually including a stop at the Blue Caves) costs €20-30 per person. Since this is a fully protected, wild beach, there are no shops, bars, or sunbeds down there. Your only expenses will be the boat ticket and any snacks bought at the port before setting off.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Check the access rules", text: "Visitors often warn that, due to the risk of rockfall from the cliffs, authorities sometimes ban landing on the sand — in which case boats just stop in the bay for swimming straight from the boat." }, { titlu: "The water colour is real", text: "Every visitor confirms that the bright blue shade isn't an editing trick — it looks exactly like the photos." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Choose an early departure from Porto Vromi, around 08:30-09:00. You'll reach the bay before the big cruise boats bring in hundreds of tourists at once, giving you a chance to enjoy the place in peace." }],
  },
  "Plaja Porto Katsiki Lefkada": {
    scurt: "Leaving Zakynthos behind, we start exploring the famous island of Lefkada with its very emblem: Porto Katsiki. This is one of the most spectacular and dramatic beaches in the entire world. A long strip of snow-white pebbles is squeezed at the foot of a vertical, huge, imposing limestone cliff. The Ionian Sea here takes on a uniquely milky-blue colour, electric in its intensity, that seems almost unreal. The scenery has a wild grandeur that will take your breath away from the very first glance.",
    cumAjungi: "Porto Katsiki sits in the south-western corner of Lefkada. The road is fully paved but a genuine challenge — narrow, full of tight bends, hairpins and steep descents through mountain villages. Public buses don't run efficient routes here, so a rental car is essential to arrive safely. Up on the plateau above the cliff there are a few large private car parks (around €10/day). From the car park, you reach the beach by descending roughly 100 sturdy concrete steps.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes are a must", text: "The beach is made of round white pebbles that can be quite painful underfoot and get very hot. You'll walk over pebbles into the sea as well." }, { titlu: "Be careful in the water", text: "The sea drops off extremely quickly (just two steps from shore), and in the afternoon big waves and strong currents can form. Not a beach recommended for unsupervised kids." }, { titlu: "A backpack instead of hand luggage", text: "Going down — and especially back up — the 100 steps with heavy bags is tiring; a backpack keeps your hands free for the railing." }],
    preturi: "Renting a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs €25-35 a day, among the priciest on the island. The canteens and tavernas above the cliff have a clever system: you can order food (gyros, burgers, salads) and drinks by phone or app, and the waiters bring your order right down to your sunbed. A frappe costs €4, and a quick lunch runs around €10-14.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Don't sit right against the cliff", text: "Visitors and authorities consistently warn about the risk of rockfall from the vertical cliff face, so it's much safer to set up your umbrella or sunbed near the water's edge." }, { titlu: "The sunset is spectacular", text: "Everyone raves about the moment the evening sun paints the huge limestone cliff in warm shades of orange and gold." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive very early, ideally before 09:00. You'll get a spot in the first car park by the stairs, find the sea calm as a swimming pool, and be able to soak in the grandeur of the place before dozens of cruise boats bring in thousands of tourists from Nidri starting around 11:00." }],
  },
  "Plaja Simos Elafonisos": {
    scurt: "Simos Beach consistently ranks among Europe's most beautiful beaches, and it's a genuine wonder of nature. Located on the small island of Elafonisos off the southern Peloponnese, Simos is a huge figure-eight-shaped beach formed by two twin bays set back to back, separated by a long tongue of fine, powder-soft pinkish-white sand. The water is such a bright, clear light turquoise that the bay feels like a tropical swimming pool plucked straight out of the Caribbean.",
    cumAjungi: "To reach this paradise, you definitely need a car to drive to the small port of Pounta in southern Laconia — the mainland road is fully paved. From Pounta, a short local ferry (just a 10-minute crossing) carries cars directly to Elafonisos island. Once you disembark, it's only 4km more along a paved dune road to the huge car park behind Simos beach. A car is vital for hauling family luggage and umbrellas onto the island. Beach parking is free.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The entire bay's seabed is covered exclusively with fine, soft, clean sand, so the risk of stepping on anything sharp is zero." }, { titlu: "Your own umbrella and mat", text: "Since the beach is huge and ecologically protected, the organised sections cover only limited areas, leaving the rest of the beach with unlimited space for those who want to settle right on the dunes." }, { titlu: "Good polarised sunglasses", text: "The white sand reflects the strong midday light intensely." }],
    preturi: "A ferry ticket for car and passengers costs around €15-20 one way. On the organised sections of the beach, a set of two sunbeds runs about €15-20 a day. A frappe costs €4, and behind the beach there's an excellent family-run taverna where a full lunch will cost you around €12-15 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A tropical paradise in Europe", text: "Every visitor is blown away by the stunning water colour and the fine sand with its pink shimmer." }, { titlu: "You never feel crowded", text: "Tourists appreciate the beach's impressive size, giving you huge personal space even in August." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive at the beach around 09:15 in the morning. The bay is incredibly calm in the early part of the day. Walk the paths between the two twin bays to admire the large sand dunes and the rare plants protected by law." }],
  },
  "Plaja Elafonisi Chania": {
    scurt: "Elafonisi is a genuine wonder of nature and one of the most spectacular beaches in the entire Mediterranean. Set in the south-western corner of Crete, it's a huge exotic lagoon world-famous for its fine sand with pink hues, caused by millions of crushed seashells. The Libyan Sea here has an unreal electric-turquoise shade and is extremely warm. A thin strip of sand, covered by very shallow water, connects the mainland to a small ecologically protected island, creating the scenery of a perfect tropical pool.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach lies roughly 75km south-west of Chania. The long distance and mountainous terrain make public transport fairly rigid, with only one bus a day, which fills up completely. A rental car is absolutely necessary to travel comfortably and at your own pace. The road crosses the island through gorgeous mountain passes and is fully paved, though winding. Behind the dunes there's a huge parking area (part of it a paid municipal lot, around €5, and free ground areas), just a few minutes' walk from the water.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The whole lagoon's seabed is covered exclusively with fine, soft, clean sand, with an extremely gentle, pleasant slope underfoot." }, { titlu: "Your own umbrella and a thick mat (optional)", text: "Although there's a large organised sunbed area, it fills up instantly. The rest of the beach and the island offer unlimited space for towels, but pitching your own umbrella on the protected island is not allowed." }, { titlu: "Good polarised sunglasses", text: "The pinkish-white sand reflects the strong midday light intensely." }],
    preturi: "In the organised areas, a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €15-20 a day. Behind the beach there are a few large kiosks where you can buy a frappe (€4), a large bottle of water (€1.50), or a quick sandwich (€6-8). Public toilets cost around €1.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A tropical paradise in Europe", text: "Every review praises the unique turquoise shades of the water and the pink sparkle of the sand at the water's edge." }, { titlu: "Gets seriously crowded by afternoon", text: "Visitors warn that from around 11:00, hundreds of tour buses arrive at once, and the beach becomes very busy." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive at the car park very early, ideally before 08:45. You'll find the lagoon perfectly still, flat as a mirror, and be able to wade across the shallow water to the island in complete peace. Be sure to cross past the island's dunes toward the open sea, where you'll find small, intimate coves of rare beauty." }],
  },
  "Laguna Balos Kissamos": {
    scurt: "Balos is one of the most famous, photographed, and spectacular locations in the entire world. Set in the north-western corner of Crete, Balos is an exotic lagoon with fine sand, distinctive pink hues (from millions of crushed shells), and extremely shallow, warm, calm water ranging from light green to electric blue. It's a genuine tropical paradise in the middle of the Mediterranean.",
    cumAjungi: "Getting to Balos is quite the adventure. You have two options: the ferry from Kissamos (which ties you to a fixed schedule) or driving. If you want full freedom, a car is the best option, but be warned — the last 8km are an unpaved forest and rock track, fairly rough going. From the upper car park, you'll need to hike down about 20-30 minutes in the sun. Having a car means you can rest as soon as you climb back up the trail. Parking is free or involves a small environmental fee (around €1-2).",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Comfortable trainers", text: "These will come in very handy for the hike from the car park down to the beach, and especially for the climb back up." }, { titlu: "Sun hat and plenty of water", text: "There's no natural shade at all along the trail, and the Cretan sun is strong from early morning." }, { titlu: "No water shoes needed in the lagoon", text: "Inside the lagoon, the seabed is exclusively fine, soft sand that's very pleasant underfoot." }],
    preturi: "There's a small snack kiosk near the car park and a beach bar set up in season, but prices are steep. Water or a soft drink costs around €4-5. A set of two sunbeds with an umbrella rents for €20-30, and spots fill up instantly.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "The view from above is breathtaking", text: "Everyone recommends taking photos from the trail before descending, since that's where the lagoon's colour contrast shows best." }, { titlu: "The drive is tough but worth it", text: "Visitors warn to drive very slowly on the unpaved section." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive at the car park before 09:00 in the morning. You'll avoid the crowds and find the lagoon calm, before the big cruise boats from Kissamos bring in hundreds of tourists at once around 11:30." }],
  },
  "Kleftiko Milos": {
    scurt: "Kleftiko isn't a traditional beach, but a monumental complex of volcanic rocks, white stone arches, and spectacular caves rising straight out of the Libyan Sea. In the past, this hidden spot served as a refuge and secret base for pirates who raided ships in the Mediterranean. The water is legendarily clear, in shades of milky turquoise and emerald, and it's considered the most spectacular snorkelling and diving spot on the whole island.",
    cumAjungi: "Kleftiko sits in the island's south-western corner and is reachable almost exclusively by sea, via organised boat trips. Even so, you'll need a car to reach the main port in Adamas or the southern departure bay (Provatas Beach), from where boats leave daily. The roads to the ports are paved and quick. There's also a tough overland trail down through the mountains to Kleftiko, but it requires a 4x4 and a long, unmarked, potentially dangerous hike under the sun.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Snorkel mask and tube are essential", text: "You'll swim right through the pirate caves and under the huge stone arches; underwater visibility is absolutely stunning." }, { titlu: "Waterproof action camera", text: "The underwater scenery and white rocks make for incredible footage you'll definitely want to capture." }, { titlu: "Water-resistant sunscreen", text: "You'll spend a lot of time swimming out in the open, straight off the boat." }],
    preturi: "A full-day boat or catamaran trip to Kleftiko (often including lunch on board, drinks, and snorkelling gear) costs €40-70 per person, depending on the type of vessel. Down at the cave complex itself, there are no shops or facilities of any kind on land.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Milos's number-one experience", text: "Every review agrees that a holiday on Milos isn't complete without a boat tour to Kleftiko." }, { titlu: "Swimming through the caves is magical", text: "Visitors are fascinated by how sunlight streams through the rock openings, shifting the water's colour underwater." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Choose a tour on a smaller boat or small sailboat that departs early, around 08:30. Smaller vessels can go much deeper into the narrow caves, letting you explore spots the big cruise boats can't reach." }],
  },
  "Plaja Myrtiotissa Corfu": {
    scurt: "Myrtiotissa is often described as one of the most isolated, wild, and charming hidden beaches on Corfu. Squeezed between huge limestone cliffs covered in lush, deep-green vegetation, this small beach offers fine silvery sand and extremely clean, transparent water. The spot has kept a bohemian, laid-back feel, historically known on the island as a partly naturist area for those seeking a total connection with unspoiled nature.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach lies on the west coast, right between the villages of Pelekas and Vatos. Public transport is completely non-existent for this secluded spot. You absolutely need a car to cover the main road, followed by a particularly steep, narrow secondary descent full of tight bends. Our tip is to leave your car for free at the dirt car park by the historic Myrtiotissa Monastery (halfway down the slope) and walk the last 300 metres, rather than risk getting your car stuck on the very steep stretch near the sand.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Your own beach umbrella", text: "The commercially organised area is minimal or non-existent depending on the month. Most of the space is completely free for towels." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "The large rocks bordering the bay continue underwater, creating spectacular channels full of small fish, great for exploring." }, { titlu: "A light backpack for the hike", text: "It will keep your hands free during the steep walk down and back up to the car." }],
    preturi: "Beach access is free. There's a small beach kiosk where you can occasionally rent sunbeds for €10-12 a set, or buy water or a frappe for €3-4. Near the monastery up top there's a small family taverna where a Greek salad or a portion of souvlaki costs around €8-11.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A hidden gem", text: "Visitors praise the wild beauty of the greenery-covered cliffs and the stunning clarity of the water." }, { titlu: "The drive needs your full attention", text: "Many reviews warn that the final slope is one of the steepest on Corfu and recommend walking down if you don't have a powerful car." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Visit in the morning, around 09:00-11:30. The sun lights the western bay directly then, making the water look completely transparent. While you're there, visit the historic 14th-century Myrtiotissa Monastery, a picturesque, peaceful spot with olive trees right above the sea." }],
  },
  "Plaja Lindos Lindos": {
    scurt: "Lindos Beach (also known as Megali Paralia) is one of the most spectacular, history-rich spots in Greece. Set in a perfectly sheltered natural bay, the beach sits right below the famous whitewashed village of Lindos and its ancient acropolis perched on the rock above. The sand is fine and golden, and the sea is incredibly warm, clean, and calm — so still it feels like a giant open-air swimming pool set against a backdrop of rare historic beauty.",
    cumAjungi: "Lindos sits on the east coast, about 50km south of Rhodes Town. Buses connect it to the capital, but in summer the journey is tiring and the schedule limits you. A rental car gives you total freedom and comfort on a fast, fully paved road. The big challenge in Lindos is parking: the village itself is pedestrian-only, so you leave the car up in the large hillside car parks (some free, others around €5-7), then walk down to the beach along a paved path.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The whole bay's seabed is covered in soft, extremely fine sand, making it a pleasure to walk barefoot through the water." }, { titlu: "Sun hat and high SPF protection", text: "The bay is sheltered from the wind, which means midday temperatures can get very high and the heat is felt strongly." }, { titlu: "Comfortable clothes and walking shoes", text: "After a few hours on the beach, it's practically a must to climb the narrow streets of Lindos village or visit the ancient acropolis." }],
    preturi: "Renting a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €15-20 a day. Right behind the beach there are charming tavernas serving excellent food. A frappe costs €4, a cold beer is €4.50, and a full meal based on fresh fish or traditional dishes runs around €15-18 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Great for little ones", text: "Parents consistently praise the extremely gentle entry into the water, which stays shallow and warm for a long stretch from the shore." }, { titlu: "A postcard-worthy view", text: "Every tourist is captivated by the sight of the acropolis dominating the sky right above the sunbeds." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive around 09:00 in the morning. You'll find parking much closer to the village and get the pick of the sunbeds. For even more peace and quiet, head to the next bay over, called Pallas Beach, in the same area, where the atmosphere is a touch more secluded." }],
  },
  "Plaja Gerakas Zakynthos": {
    scurt: "Set at the southern tip of the Vassilikos peninsula, Gerakas is considered one of the most beautiful, clean, and protected beaches on Zakynthos. It's a long, wide strip of warm golden sand, flanked by clay hills and unusual rock formations. The beach is part of the National Marine Park and is a preferred nesting site for the famous Caretta-Caretta sea turtles, which is why it has remained completely unspoilt — no modern buildings or noisy water sports allowed.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach lies about 18km south of Zakynthos Town. The road is fully paved, winds pleasantly through olive groves, and is a nice drive. Local buses run rarely and on a rigid schedule, hard to fit around a relaxed beach day. A rental car gets you there quickly, and you can leave it in a large, free public car park about 200m from the beach. From there, a wooden boardwalk built specifically to protect the turtle nests in the dunes leads down to the sea.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Your own beach umbrella", text: "There's a small area where park volunteers rent eco-friendly wooden umbrellas, but they run out fast. Bring your own, but note that pitching it in the sand is only allowed in marked zones, to avoid disturbing turtle eggs." }, { titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The seabed is covered entirely in fine, clean sand, and the entry into the water is extremely gentle." }, { titlu: "Swimming goggles", text: "The water is warm, calm, and very clear — great for long swims." }],
    preturi: "Renting a simple eco-friendly umbrella costs around €5-7 a day (there are no plastic sunbeds here, just small folding chairs or a towel on the sand). At the trailhead there's a turtle information centre and a few excellent tavernas. A warm meal with traditional dishes will cost around €12-15 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Strict rules, but necessary ones", text: "Visitors mention that park volunteers give you a quick briefing on arrival and explain the rules (no pointed umbrellas outside the permitted zones, and no staying on the beach after sunset)." }, { titlu: "Total peace and quiet", text: "Widely praised for the lack of loud music and motorboats." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Come in the morning around 09:00. You'll catch an incredibly calm atmosphere, and if you're lucky, you might see volunteers marking new turtle nests made overnight. Also, avoid touching or climbing the clay hills at the end of the beach — it's forbidden, as the structure is extremely fragile and can collapse." }],
  },
  "Plaja Laganas Zakynthos": {
    scurt: "Laganas Beach is the epicentre of fun, nightlife, and vibrant tourism on Zakynthos. Stretching an impressive 9km along a huge bay in the south of the island, it's made of fine sand and lined with an unbroken row of modern beach bars, clubs, hotels, and tavernas. It's the place where music pulses all day long and the atmosphere is always festive — a favourite destination for young travellers from across Europe.",
    cumAjungi: "Laganas is just 8km from the island's capital and very close to the airport. The road is straight, flat, and busy. Though the resort is fairly well connected by public transport, a rental car gives you a huge advantage: parking in the centre of Laganas is a nightmare due to the crowds. With a car, you can head toward the far end of the beach (the Kalamaki or Agios Sostis area), where you can park for free on dirt lots behind the bars and access a much airier part of the bay.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Budget for a boat rental", text: "Laganas is the island's best spot to rent a small motorboat (no licence needed) to go looking for Caretta-Caretta turtles or visit Marathonisi Island (Turtle Island)." }, { titlu: "Headphones (if you want peace and quiet)", text: "Being very commercial, the beach has bar speakers running constantly." }, { titlu: "No special footwear needed", text: "The entry into the water is extremely gentle, entirely over fine sand, staying shallow for a long stretch out." }],
    preturi: "With so much competition, prices are affordable. Most beach bars give you a free set of two sunbeds with an umbrella if you order drinks worth a minimum amount (around €10-15 total). A large cocktail costs €7-9, a frappe is €3.50, and a quick lunch (gyros or club sandwich) runs €5-8.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "The perfect spot for partygoers", text: "Young travellers consistently praise the nightlife and the clubs just steps from the sand." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "If you want to experience the famous nightlife, come to the beach in the late afternoon, stay for a sunset cocktail, then move to the resort's main street, which becomes fully pedestrian and buzzing after 21:00." }],
  },
  "Plaja Banana Beach Zakynthos": {
    scurt: "Banana Beach is the largest and widest sandy beach on the whole island of Zakynthos. Set on the Vassilikos peninsula, this impressive beach offers an exotic setting with fine golden sand and clear water that turns spectacular shades of turquoise in the sun. It's a lively, fully organised spot where modern beachfront bars blend seamlessly with huge open space. If you want comfort, good music, and plenty of room, Banana Beach is the place.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach lies about 14km from Zakynthos Town. Although buses run toward Vassilikos, their schedule is unpredictable and drops you well short of the shore. A rental car is by far the best option. The access road is fully paved, and from the main road you drop straight into a huge dirt car park under trees, where you can leave your car completely free of charge. The large parking area means you'll never stress about finding a spot, whatever the time.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Budget for water sports", text: "Banana Beach is famous for having the island's largest and best-equipped water sports centre (parasailing, flyboarding, jet skis, or inflatable towables)." }, { titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The seabed is an unbroken stretch of fine sand, ideal for sensitive feet, with an extremely gentle entry." }, { titlu: "Polarised sunglasses", text: "The huge expanse of golden sand reflects the midday light strongly." }],
    preturi: "Renting a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €15-25, depending on the row and the beach bar. A frappe costs €4, a cocktail runs €9-11, and a quick club sandwich or burger at the cosy restaurants behind the beach costs €10-12.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "You never feel crowded", text: "Tourists praise the beach's size — even on the busiest August days, there's enough personal space for everyone." }, { titlu: "Excellent service", text: "Reviews often mention the quality of bars like Casa Playa and the presence of clean showers and changing rooms." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive around 10:00 to grab a spot in the front row of sunbeds. If you catch a day with a light southerly breeze, the sea will have small, fun waves — great for jumping in." }],
  },
  "Plaja Egremni Lefkada": {
    scurt: "Egremni is Lefkada's other legendary beach, located north of Porto Katsiki. It's a huge, imposing stretch of white sand mixed with fine pebbles, nearly 3km long, guarded by a tall, steep limestone cliff. Many consider the sea colour here to be the most beautiful in all of Greece — an electric, milky, incredibly intense blue. Thanks to its massive size, Egremni keeps a much wilder, freer, and airier feel than Porto Katsiki.",
    cumAjungi: "Set on the south-west coast, Egremni was accessible only by boat for years after the 2015 earthquake destroyed its stairway. Today, both the road and the steps have been fully rebuilt! You definitely need a car — the road is paved up to a point, followed by a dirt stretch where you can leave your car on the roadside (or in an improvised car park for €5-10). From there, it's about a 1km walk on a car-free road, followed by a descent of over 400 metal steps suspended on the cliff.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Plenty of still water and snacks", text: "Climbing back up the 400 steps in the sun is a real physical test. Bring hydration reserves!" }, { titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Very useful for walking comfortably over the fine pebbles on the shore and in the water." }, { titlu: "Your own beach umbrella", text: "Most of this huge beach is completely wild and unorganised, with no natural shade at all." }],
    preturi: "Beach access is free. In high season, there's a small organised area with sunbeds near the stairs, where a set costs around €20-25. There's also a small caravan/kiosk at the base of the stairs selling cold water or juice for €3-4. All other parts of the 3km-long beach are free and open to everyone.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "The effort is 100% worth it", text: "Every visitor mentions the road and the steps are exhausting on the way back, but the unreal water colour and lack of crowds make Egremni an unforgettable experience." }, { titlu: "A dramatic sea", text: "Visitors note that waves can get quite large and powerful in the afternoon." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Come in the morning, around 09:00. You'll go down the steps in shade (the huge cliff blocks the sun in the early morning) and enjoy the beach in much cooler conditions before the day's heat sets in." }],
  },
  "Plaja Kathisma Lefkada": {
    scurt: "Kathisma is the most cosmopolitan, vibrant, and longest organised beach on the island's west coast. It's a huge stretch of fine sand mixed with white pebbles, lapped by an electric-turquoise Ionian Sea. Unlike the wild beaches nearby, Kathisma is a haven of comfort: packed with modern beach bars, stylish beachfront pools, restaurants, and excellent water sports facilities.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach lies about 15km south of Lefkada Town. A rental car is by far the best option, as the road is fully paved, wide, and descends right down to the sand. The huge advantage is that you can park directly behind the beach — there's a large free public car park along the road, plus paid private ones offered by the bars (around €5-10).",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No water shoes needed on the sandy sections", text: "The sand is very pleasant across most of the beach, though pebbles can appear right at the water's edge." }, { titlu: "Budget for a paragliding flight", text: "Kathisma is famous for tandem paragliding flights that take off from the mountain behind and land right on the beach." }, { titlu: "Be very careful in the sea", text: "The sea drops off quickly, and waves here can get huge and quite rough in the second half of the day." }],
    preturi: "Renting a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €15-25, depending on the bar and how close you are to the water. A frappe costs €4, a cocktail is around €10, and a full meal at the large restaurants above the beach runs €15-20 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Excellent facilities", text: "Everyone praises the showers, changing rooms, and general cleanliness of the beach." }, { titlu: "Postcard-worthy sunsets", text: "The west-facing orientation delivers a stunning show as the sun sinks into the sea." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "For more peace, head to the far right end of the beach (facing the sea), past the large rocks in the water. That area is completely free, much less crowded, and perfect for a towel straight on the sand." }],
  },
  "Plaja Vai Lasithi": {
    scurt: "Vai Beach (officially known as Finikodasos) is one of Crete's most famous and spectacular destinations, offering scenery unique in all of Europe. What makes it famous is the huge wild Cretan palm forest (Phoenix theophrasti) that grows naturally right behind the sand, spreading over more than 20 hectares. The beach itself is a gorgeous crescent of fine golden sand, washed by a warm, clear, brilliant turquoise sea. It's a true exotic paradise corner that will make you feel like you're on a tropical island.",
    cumAjungi: "Vai sits in the north-eastern corner of the island, about 24km from Sitia and 94km from Agios Nikolaos. Due to its remote location at the island's edge, public transport is extremely rare and impractical. A rental car is absolutely essential for covering the fast, paved road. The site has a huge public car park on dirt ground, with an environmental fee (around €3-5 a day). Car access is very easy, with parking just a minute's walk from the first palm trees.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The seabed is clean, entirely fine and pleasant sand, with a gentle entry." }, { titlu: "A charged camera or phone", text: "A short walk up steps on the rock on the right side of the beach leads to a superb viewpoint, where you can take the famous overhead photo of the palm forest and turquoise sea." }, { titlu: "Good polarised sunglasses", text: "The golden sand and palm leaves reflect the midday sun strongly." }],
    preturi: "As a major top-tier tourist attraction, the beach is fully organised. Renting a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €15-25 a day, depending on the row. A large restaurant and snack bar operate right at the edge of the forest. A frappe costs €4, a beer is €4.50, and a quick lunch or a fresh salad runs €10-14.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "An unreal tropical oasis", text: "Every visitor is amazed by the unique beauty of the palm forest reaching all the way to the sand." }, { titlu: "Gets crowded at midday", text: "Reviews often warn that from 11:00 onward, lots of cars and buses arrive and the beach becomes fairly busy." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive at the car park around 09:00 in the morning. You'll get a shaded parking spot under the trees, a front-row sunbed, and total quiet in the forest. A local tip: from the top of the viewpoint rock, the path continues down the other side to a second beach (Psili Ammos), which is completely wild, unorganised, and much quieter." }],
  },
  "Red Beach Heraklion": {
    scurt: "Red Beach (or Kokkini Ammos) is one of the most spectacular, isolated, and unusual beaches in Crete. Tucked into a picturesque bay just south of Matala, it will take your breath away with its dramatic setting: the sand is an intense reddish-copper colour, and the bay is flanked by steep ochre sandstone cliffs. The sea has rare clarity, taking on brilliant emerald-green shades against the red sand. It's a fully wild beach, famous for its free-spirited, unconventional vibe.",
    cumAjungi: "There's no direct road access to the beach, as it's protected by a rocky mountain. You'll need a car to reach Matala, where you can leave your vehicle in the large car park in the resort centre (around €3-5 a day). From there, the adventure begins on foot: a demanding 25-30 minute hike over the hill. The path starts behind the village, is steep, rocky, and only partly marked, requiring real effort, especially on the way back up.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Comfortable trainers", text: "The path over the hill is full of loose stones and stretches where you need to scramble slightly over rock. Avoid basic flip-flops for this trail entirely!" }, { titlu: "A backpack with plenty of still water", text: "Resources down in the bay are extremely limited, and the effort of the hike under a blazing sun will dehydrate you quickly." }, { titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "Once you're down, the reddish sand is fine and soft, and the entry into the sea is clean, free of large stones." }],
    preturi: "Beach access is free. In high season, a local opens a small improvised wooden shack right on the sand (the famous Yannis Mojito bar), where you can buy cold drinks or his famous cocktails for €7-9. Occasionally there are a few rustic wooden sunbeds to rent for around €10-15 a set.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A completely different place", text: "Visitors are fascinated by the unique sand colour and the artwork carved by visitors into the rocks at the edge of the beach." }, { titlu: "The trail is tiring but worth it", text: "Every review warns that climbing back over the hill at midday is very hard due to the heat." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Set off early in the morning, around 08:30. You'll cross the hill in pleasant temperatures while the path is still partly shaded, and reach the red beach in complete peace before other tourists arrive. Note that a good part of the beach is traditionally used by naturist visitors — the spot is known for tolerance and mutual respect." }],
  },
  "Plaja Falassarna Chania": {
    scurt: "Falassarna is one of Crete's largest, cleanest, and most acclaimed beaches, regularly awarded the prestigious Blue Flag. Set on the west coast, it's actually a series of 5 huge beaches, all covered in fine, light-golden sand with a pinkish shimmer. The sea has legendary clarity, in a deep turquoise colour. Thanks to its massive size, Falassarna offers a rare sense of open space and total freedom, making it the perfect beach for anyone who loves comfort and plenty of room.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach lies about 52km west of Chania and 15km from Kissamos. Although a few regional buses run, a rental car gives you total comfort, with a modern, fully paved, fast coastal road. A big advantage at Falassarna is parking: behind each stretch of beach there are huge public dirt lots where you can park completely free, just steps from the sand — one of the easiest access points on the island by car.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The whole beach and seabed are made entirely of fine, pleasant sand, with zero risk of stepping on anything sharp." }, { titlu: "Budget for water sports or volleyball", text: "Falassarna is very well equipped, with beach volleyball nets and excellent centres for renting surfboards or jet skis." }, { titlu: "Good sunglasses", text: "The huge stretch of sand reflects the strong midday light intensely." }],
    preturi: "In the areas run by modern beachfront bars, renting a set of two sunbeds costs around €15-25 a day, depending on the row. A frappe costs €4, a cold beer is €4.50, and a full dinner at the excellent traditional tavernas on the hills behind the beach costs around €13-16 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Huge space and comfort", text: "Every visitor praises the impressive width of the beach, mentioning you never feel crowded, even on the busiest August weekends." }, { titlu: "Watch out for waves", text: "Reviews mention that, being fully open to the west, in the second half of the day the wind can create big, fun waves — ideal for jumping." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Stay on the beach or at a taverna on the hill until late. Falassarna offers one of the most spectacular, clean, and stunning sunsets in all of Crete, the sun sinking straight into the open sea. For more peace, choose the northern section called Small Beach, more sheltered by the rocks." }],
  },
  "Plaja Sarakiniko Milos": {
    scurt: "Sarakiniko is one of Greece's most famous and photographed beaches, with a landscape that looks like the surface of the moon. There's no classic sand here, just a spectacular expanse of pristine white volcanic rock, shaped by wind and waves into flowing forms and narrow canyons. The sea has a deep electric-blue shade in contrast to the blinding white of the rock. It's a place of raw beauty that will make you feel like you've landed on another planet.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is on the north coast of Milos. Public transport reaches it rarely, and the rigid schedule will make you miss the best hours of the day. A rental car is absolutely necessary to explore this spectacular area at your own pace. The access road is fully paved, and you can park for free in a large dirt lot right above the rock formations. From there, it's only a 2-3 minute walk.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Good polarised sunglasses", text: "The white volcanic rock reflects sunlight extremely strongly, just like snow in winter." }, { titlu: "Your own umbrella or beach tent", text: "Sarakiniko is 100% public and unorganised. There are no sunbeds, bars, or natural shade." }, { titlu: "Grippy footwear (trainers)", text: "Although the rocks look smooth, walking in basic flip-flops on the polished, steep shapes can be slippery and dangerous." }],
    preturi: "Access to the rocks and parking are completely free. In high season, a food truck sets up in the parking area, where you can buy cold water or a frappe for €3.50-4. There are no other commercial costs down in the bay.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Magazine-worthy photos", text: "Everyone recommends exploring the small caves and tunnels carved into the white rock — incredibly photogenic spots." }, { titlu: "Cliff jumping", text: "The braver visitors praise the high points where you can jump straight into the deep, clean water." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive either at sunrise (for a mystical, totally empty atmosphere) or after 17:00. The warm sunset light paints the white rocks in pale shades of pink and gold, and if you stay after dark on full-moon nights, the scenery becomes truly otherworldly." }],
  },
  "Plaja Firiplaka Milos": {
    scurt: "Firiplaka is one of the longest, most comfortable, and spectacular beaches on Milos's southern coast. Unlike the tiny coves nearby, it offers a wide strip of fine, silvery sand, majestically flanked by huge volcanic rocks layered in warm shades of yellow, pink, and ochre. The sea is warm, rare in its transparency, and has a light turquoise shade — a gentle entry into the Libyan Sea, perfect for total relaxation.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach sits right next to Tsigrado beach, in the south of the island. Public transport is rare, with stops fairly far from the shore. A rental car gives you full comfort. The final stretch of the secondary access road is packed dirt, flat and easy to drive. Parking is free, on the roadside above the beach, but due to its popularity, spots close to the access path fill up fast after 10:00. A gentle dirt path leads down to the beach.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The seabed is clean, entirely covered in fine sand that's pleasant to the touch, with zero risk of stepping on anything sharp." }, { titlu: "Good sunglasses", text: "The colourful volcanic rocks reflect the strong midday light straight onto the sand." }, { titlu: "A camera", text: "A huge boulder that's fallen into the sea right in the middle of the beach makes for a stunning photo backdrop." }],
    preturi: "The beach is partly organised. A set of two sunbeds with an umbrella in the area run by the eco-friendly beach bar costs around €15-20 a day. A frappe costs €4, cold water is €1.50, and quick snacks (sandwiches, salads) run €7-9. The rest of the beach is completely free for towels.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "The most comfortable beach in the south", text: "Every visitor praises the perfect balance between the wild volcanic scenery and the presence of comfortable sunbeds." }, { titlu: "Great for families", text: "The gentle entry into the calm sea is a strong point often mentioned by parents." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive around 09:15 in the morning to get a parking spot close to the path. For more privacy, walk toward the far right end of the beach (past the huge rock in the water). That area is completely wild, quiet, and away from the bar's music." }],
  },
  "Canal d'Amour Sidari": {
    scurt: "Canal d'Amour (Canal of Love) is one of the most unique and unusual geological formations in all of Greece. Located in the resort of Sidari, the beach is made of layered yellow sandstone that wind and waves have sculpted into narrow channels, grottoes, and spectacular arches. The beach itself is tiny, set at the end of a turquoise-water channel. The spot is legendary and draws thousands of couples in love every summer.",
    cumAjungi: "Sidari sits in the extreme north of Corfu, about 36km from the capital. The main road is paved but crosses the mountains in the island's centre, with many narrow stretches and tight bends. A rental car gives you huge comfort for this long drive at your own pace. Near the channel there are small paid private car parks (around €4-5 a day) and free spots on the side streets behind the hotels.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "A mat or thick towel", text: "Since the beach is tiny, most visitors settle right on the flat yellow sandstone platforms on the rocks." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "The soft sandstone continues underwater, creating fascinating underwater tunnels you can swim through." }, { titlu: "Don't leave valuables unattended", text: "The rocky area gets busy, so it's worth having a small waterproof backpack to carry with you." }],
    preturi: "Access to the natural landmark is free. On the rocks, a few rows of sunbeds are offered by bars for around €15 a set. A frappe costs €4, and a portion of pancakes or a quick snack at the bar pools behind is around €6-8.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "The legend lives on", text: "Everyone mentions the local myth that couples who swim through the channel together stay in love for life, and single visitors will find their soulmate." }, { titlu: "Very crowded and noisy", text: "Reviews mention the spot is very touristy and tight, getting stifling by midday." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Come in the late afternoon, around 17:30. Most tour buses have already left, the yellow rocks take on a warm orange glow in the sunset light, and the atmosphere becomes much more romantic and photo-friendly." }],
  },
  "Plaja Voidokilia Pylos": {
    scurt: "Voidokilia is one of the most spectacular, famous, and Instagram-worthy beaches in all of Greece. Picture a perfect crescent-shaped bay (or the Greek letter Omega), where two large rocky headlands narrow the opening to the sea, fully sheltering the water from waves. The sand is fine as talc, and the water is warm, very shallow, and an otherworldly turquoise. As a protected nature reserve of huge ecological and historical importance, the beach has remained completely untouched by commerce.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach lies on the Peloponnese's west coast, in the Messinia region, near the town of Pylos. Public transport doesn't reach this isolated nature reserve at all, so a car is absolutely essential. The final stretch of road is partly paved and partly narrow packed dirt, winding past the Gialova salt lake. Drive slowly and you can park for free right in the dirt lot behind the sand dunes, just a minute's walk from the beach.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Your own beach umbrella and tent", text: "Voidokilia is 100% public and unorganised. There are no bars, sunbeds, or kiosks on the sand. Come fully equipped with your own shade." }, { titlu: "A well-stocked cooler", text: "Bring plenty of cold still water and snacks, as the nearest shop is in the village of Gialova, a few kilometres away." }, { titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The whole bay's seabed is covered exclusively with fine, soft, clean sand, with zero risk of stepping on anything sharp." }],
    preturi: "Beach access and parking behind the dunes are completely free. There are no vendors on the sand, so your expenses here will be zero. For a warm lunch after the beach, it's best to drive 10 minutes to the charming tavernas on the seafront in the neighbouring village of Gialova.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A breathtaking landscape", text: "Every review praises the bay's perfect shape and the stunning water colour, like an exotic lagoon." }, { titlu: "Climb up to the castle for the view", text: "Many tourists recommend a short but steep hike up to the ruins of the old Paleokastro castle on the rock above the beach, which offers the best view of the bay's perfect Omega shape." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive at the car park around 09:00 in the morning. You'll find the access path quieter, the sea completely flat like a mirror, and enjoy the bay's peacefulness before the sun gets too strong. Please respect the protective signs around the sand dunes, home to rare plants protected by law." }],
  },
  "Plaja Costa Navarino Pylos": {
    scurt: "Costa Navarino beach (often associated with The Dunes beach or the beaches of Navarino Bay) is one of the most spectacular, long, and exclusive coastal destinations in the Messinia region of the Peloponnese. It's a huge stretch of fine, warm golden sand, caressed by the deep, clean waters of the Ionian Sea. Flanked by ecologically protected sand dunes and vast olive groves, the beach strikes a perfect balance between world-class resort luxury and untouched wild nature.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach lies on the Peloponnese's west coast, near the historic town of Pylos. The long distance from the main airports in Athens or Kalamata makes a car absolutely essential for travelling in this region. The main road is fully paved and modern, offering stunning mountain and sea views. For day visitors, there are well-signposted public access points where you can park completely free on the large dirt areas behind the sand dunes, just a minute's walk from the beach.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The whole beach and seabed are covered exclusively with fine, soft, clean sand, making the entry into the open sea a real pleasure." }, { titlu: "Your own beach umbrella (optional)", text: "Since the beach is huge, the commercial organised sections only cover limited areas near the resorts, leaving the rest of the beach with unlimited space for towels." }, { titlu: "Good polarised sunglasses", text: "The long stretch of sand reflects the midday light strongly." }],
    preturi: "In the areas run by the luxury beach clubs, prices are fairly steep, with a set of sunbeds costing €20-40 a day depending on the facilities. That said, access to the free sections of the beach is completely free. A frappe costs around €4-5, and a meal at the excellent tavernas in nearby villages (like Gialova) costs around €15 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Immaculate natural scenery", text: "Every review praises how well the sand dunes are protected and maintained, giving the beach a very select, clean feel." }, { titlu: "Memorable sunsets", text: "Visitors are captivated by the sight of the sun setting directly into the open sea, painting the sky in stunning shades of red and gold." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive around 09:30 in the morning, when the sea is usually extremely calm. If you're into history or nature, use the car in the afternoon to drive 10 minutes to the famous perfect-crescent Voidokilia beach or the ruins of Paleokastro castle, both right near Navarino Bay." }],
  },
  "Plaja Kavourotrypes Sithonia": {
    scurt: "Kavourotrypes (also known as Orange Beach) is arguably the most spectacular and exotic spot in all of Sithonia. It's not one single classic beach, but a network of intimate little coves hidden among pines and soft white limestone rocks, shaped by the waves into strange forms. The water here has such a clear, intense turquoise-emerald colour that the place feels cut straight out of an exotic island. It's a photographer's paradise, but also a favourite for those who love a bohemian vibe.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach is on Sithonia's east coast, about a 10-minute drive north of the resort town of Sarti. There's no big roadside signage, just a discreet turn onto a rough dirt track through the forest. Without a car, it's nearly impossible to find or reach it. Drive slowly, and you can leave your car completely free of charge in the shade of the pine forest behind, then it's about a 5-minute walk on narrow paths.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "The smooth white rocks continue underwater, creating small caves and channels full of fish — one of the best snorkelling spots in the region." }, { titlu: "A mat or thick towel", text: "If you don't grab a spot on the small strips of sand, the best places to sit are directly on the flat white rock platforms, where a thin towel isn't very comfortable." }, { titlu: "Comfortable walking shoes", text: "Avoid basic flip-flops for the forest and rock path, as it's steep and slippery in places." }],
    preturi: "Most of the little coves are completely free and open to everyone. There's a single organised area with one beach bar (Portokali), where a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €15-20, often as a minimum-spend arrangement. A frappe costs around €4.50, and a quick sandwich runs €6-7.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Fills up extremely fast", text: "Since the coves are small, the beach feels packed almost immediately. Visitors recommend arriving very early to grab a spot on the sand." }, { titlu: "Incredible scenery", text: "Everyone praises the contrast between the green pines, white rock, and turquoise sea." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Come before 08:30 in the morning. You'll get good parking, total peace and quiet, and be able to admire the water's clarity before it's stirred up by hundreds of tourists." }],
  },
  "Plaja Faliraki Faliraki": {
    scurt: "Faliraki Beach is the heart of entertainment and mass tourism on Rhodes. Stretching an impressive 5km along the east coast, this huge beach is made entirely of fine golden sand. The sea is clean, warm, with a gentle entry, sheltered from strong winds. Faliraki is probably the best-equipped beach on the island: an unbroken row of modern beach bars, tavernas, hotels, and shopping centres, giving it a lively, energetic atmosphere.",
    cumAjungi: "Faliraki is about 12km south of Rhodes Town. The road is a modern, wide, fully paved highway. Although it's the best-connected resort by public transport, a rental car gives you a huge advantage: since the beach is so vast, a car lets you quickly move from one end to the other, or visit the famous Faliraki Water Park (Greece's largest water park, on the nearby hill). Parking is simple and free in the large dirt lots behind the beach.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Budget for water sports", text: "Faliraki is a water sports paradise; you can try anything, from parasailing and jet skis to pedal boats and rental motorboats." }, { titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The seabed is entirely covered in fine, soft sand, with no stones or sea urchins." }, { titlu: "High-SPF sunscreen", text: "The long stretch of golden sand retains heat and reflects sunlight strongly all day long." }],
    preturi: "Heavy competition keeps prices very affordable. A set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €10-15 a day, or is included with a minimum order at the bars. A frappe costs €3.50, a quick gyros is around €4, and a full family dinner at the countless tavernas behind the beach costs around €35-45.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Top-notch facilities", text: "Every visitor praises the complete amenities: plentiful showers, toilets, changing cabins, and lifeguards along the whole beach." }, { titlu: "Excellent for kids", text: "The gentle entry and soft sand are much appreciated by parents." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "If you want to escape the loud music in the central area and want more peace, head to the southern end of the beach (the area called Kathara Beach), near the fishing harbour. The atmosphere there is much more relaxed, the sand just as fine, and the scenery with small wooden boats is very picturesque." }],
  },
  "Plaja Tsambika Archangelos": {
    scurt: "Tsambika Beach is considered one of the most beautiful, largest, and most spectacular sandy beaches on the whole island of Rhodes. It's a huge stretch of shimmering golden sand, dramatically framed by bare mountain slopes. The sea has remarkable clarity, is warm, and has a gorgeous light turquoise shade. Its landmark feature is the historic Tsambika Monastery, perched on the huge vertical cliff guarding the beach's left side, giving the spot a backdrop of real natural grandeur.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach lies about 26km south of Rhodes Town. Local buses only drop you at the main road up top, from where it's a long, tiring walk in the sun. A rental car is absolutely essential to drive comfortably right down to the shore. The secondary access road is fully paved, modern, and fast. Parking is among the easiest on the island: since the beach is so vast, there's a huge public dirt area right behind it where you can park completely free, just steps from the sunbeds.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The whole bay's seabed is made exclusively of soft, fine, clean sand, with zero risk of stepping on stones or sea urchins." }, { titlu: "Plenty of sand toys for the kids", text: "The sand quality and the extremely gentle slope into the sea make this an ideal, very safe beach for children." }, { titlu: "Budget for water sports or a mini water park", text: "There are excellent centres for renting pedal boats or trying the large inflatable water platforms." }],
    preturi: "A set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €15 a day. Behind the beach there are a few large wooden canteens and tavernas run by locals. A frappe costs €3.50, a cold beer is €4, and a quick gyros or fresh salad runs €7-10.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "An endless stretch of golden sand", text: "Every review praises the beach's size and the quality of the soft sand, calling it the perfect spot for a family relax day." }, { titlu: "A unique view from the cliff", text: "Visitors recommend driving and then climbing the 350 steps up to the hilltop monastery for a dreamlike panorama over the whole bay." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Arrive at the car park around 09:30 in the morning. The bay is incredibly quiet in the early part of the day, with the sun lighting the golden sand directly. For more free space to lay your towel, head toward the far right end of the beach, which is completely unorganised and very open." }],
  },
  "Plaja Sounion Riviera Ateniană": {
    scurt: "Sounion Beach offers an overwhelmingly beautiful historic setting, sitting right at the foot of the huge cliff on which the famous Temple of Poseidon (built in the 5th century BC) stands. The beach is tucked into a picturesque cove covered with fine golden sand and small white pebbles. The water is extremely clean, warm, and a brilliant turquoise, offering the unique experience of swimming in the Aegean Sea while admiring the ancient temple's white marble columns straight from your sunbed.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach lies at the southernmost point of Attica, about 65km from Athens. The long distance and lack of regular bus routes make a car absolutely essential for a relaxed trip. The coastal road is fully paved, modern, and offers spectacular views. Parking is free, either on the side of the secondary road leading down to the beach or in the dedicated spaces of the seafront tavernas, just a minute's walk from the water.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No water shoes needed", text: "The seabed in the central area is clean, made entirely of fine sand, with a very pleasant entry." }, { titlu: "A charged camera or phone", text: "The sight of the ancient temple on the cliff above the sunbeds is simply spectacular and an essential holiday photo." }, { titlu: "A stylish sun hat", text: "Being sheltered from strong winds, the bay gets noticeably hot at midday." }],
    preturi: "As a highly sought-after historic location, prices are mid-to-high range. A set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €15-25 a day, depending on proximity to the water. A frappe costs €4, and the excellent traditional tavernas on the seafront serve very good food. A full meal will cost around €15-20 per person.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A one-of-a-kind mythological setting", text: "Every review is captivated by the grandeur of the place and the special feeling of swimming under the sea god's watchful eye." }, { titlu: "Very safe for kids", text: "Visitors praise the gentle water gradient and the lack of big waves." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Plan your day so you're on the beach in the morning around 09:30, when the bay is calm. In the late afternoon, drive up to the Temple of Poseidon — the sunset seen from the ancient rocks is considered the most beautiful and spectacular in all of mainland Greece." }],
  },
  "Plaja Agios Gordios Corfu": {
    scurt: "Agios Gordios is one of the most spectacular and imposing beaches on Corfu's west coast. Set in a huge bay, the beach is framed by green mountains covered in pine forests and olive groves that seem to tumble into the Ionian Sea. It's a long, wide beach, made mostly of fine golden sand. Its emblematic feature is the huge Ortholithi rock, rising majestically straight out of the turquoise water on the bay's left side, giving the scene a dramatic, storybook backdrop.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach lies about 15km south-west of the capital, Corfu Town. The road crossing the island through mountain villages (like Sinarades) is fully paved but fairly narrow, full of tight bends and steep descents toward the coast. Green buses run on a rigid schedule, making a rental car the better option. Parking near the sand can be a challenge in season; there are paid private car parks close to the shore (around €5 a day) or free spots along the access road if you arrive early.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "No water shoes needed in the central area", text: "The seabed is covered with soft, very fine sand, ideal for sensitive feet, though a few stones can appear near the edges." }, { titlu: "A charged camera or phone", text: "The isolated offshore rock and the spectacular sunset make for great photo material." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "Near the large rocks at the ends of the bay, underwater life is quite active." }],
    preturi: "Renting a set of two sunbeds with an umbrella costs around €12-18 a day. Along the seafront there are numerous excellent bars and tavernas. A frappe costs €4, a gyros on the seafront is €4.50, and a full family dinner at the traditional tavernas costs around €35-45.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "Scenery that wins you over", text: "Every visitor praises the grandeur of the green mountains and the beauty of the offshore Ortholithi rock." }, { titlu: "Great for families and swimmers", text: "Tourists appreciate the fairly gentle entry into the clean sea and the beach's excellent organisation." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Stay on the beach until late. Facing due west, Agios Gordios delivers an amazing show as the sun sinks into the open sea. For more peace, head to the left end of the beach (toward the rock), where the area is more open and you can lay your towel straight on the sand." }],
  },
  "Plaja Afandou Afandou": {
    scurt: "Afandou Beach is one of the longest, most expansive beaches on Rhodes, stretching an impressive nearly 4km. Made of a mix of coarse sand and fine, wave-rounded pebbles, this huge bay is the very definition of space and freedom. Thanks to its massive size, Afandou never feels crowded, making it the ideal spot for tourists who want to escape the crowds and enjoy an extremely clean, deep, and refreshing sea.",
    cumAjungi: "The beach lies on the east coast, about 20km from Rhodes Town and very close to Faliraki. Public transport only drops you at the edge of Afandou village, from where it's over a kilometre's walk in the sun. A car is absolutely necessary to reach the shore directly. Access from the main road is fully paved, flat, and very easy. Parking is among the easiest on the island: you can leave your car completely free right behind the beach, along the long road that follows the shoreline.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Aqua shoes", text: "Highly recommended for stepping comfortably over the band of pebbles at the entry into the deeper sea." }, { titlu: "Your own beach umbrella", text: "Most of this huge beach is completely wild and unorganised, giving unlimited space for anyone who wants to lay out a towel." }, { titlu: "Snorkelling mask", text: "Since the water is extremely clear and clean, underwater visibility is excellent, especially near the rock formations at the end of the beach." }],
    preturi: "In the few organised sections near guesthouses, a set of two sunbeds costs around €10-12 a day. A few caravans and local tavernas are scattered along the coast. A large bottle of still water costs €1.50, a frappe is €3.50, and food prices are considerably lower than in Lindos.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A huge beach all to yourself", text: "Visitors are delighted at how much distance you can keep from the next tourist, even in peak summer." }, { titlu: "The water deepens quickly", text: "Reviews mention the sea gets deep after just 3-4 steps from shore, making it ideal for strong swimmers." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "Head to the far right end of the beach (the area known as Traganou), where large rocks hide spectacular sea caves. It's the most photogenic spot on the beach and offers welcome natural shade in the afternoon." }],
  },
  "Plaja Prasonisi Prasonisi": {
    scurt: "Prasonisi is a one-of-a-kind place in the world and one of Greece's most spectacular geographical attractions. At the very southern tip of Rhodes, Prasonisi is a peninsula (or an island connected to the mainland by a long strip of fine sand) where two different seas meet: the Aegean and the Mediterranean. The phenomenon creates a stunning contrast: on one side of the sand spit the sea has big waves and strong wind, making it a world-class windsurfing haven, while on the other side the water is completely flat, calm, and still.",
    cumAjungi: "Prasonisi lies about 90km south of Rhodes Town. Due to the long distance and its isolated location, public transport is almost non-existent. A car is absolutely essential to reach this end-of-the-world spot. The island's main road is fully paved, flat, and very straight in its final stretch. Once you arrive, you can drive right onto the wide sand strip at the base of the beach, where parking is huge and completely free. Just be careful not to park too close to the water, to avoid getting stuck in wet sand at high tide.",
    echipament: [{ titlu: "Polarised sunglasses and a scarf", text: "The wind blows strongly here almost constantly, kicking up fine sand, so eye protection is essential." }, { titlu: "A kite or sturdy beach gear", text: "Even if you don't windsurf, simply walking the sand spit where the two seas meet is a memorable experience." }, { titlu: "No large inflatable mattresses", text: "Due to the strong wind on the Aegean side, there's a real risk of being carried out to sea." }],
    preturi: "Beach access is free. There are a few sunbed sections in the sheltered area, where a set costs around €15. A small tourist village has grown up behind the beach, full of windsurfing schools, gear shops, and tavernas. A full lunch costs around €12-15 per person, and renting windsurf or kitesurf gear starts at €40 an hour.",
    turisti: [{ titlu: "A show put on by nature", text: "Every review praises the unique feeling of standing on a strip of sand with big waves on your right and a sea as calm as a lake on your left." }, { titlu: "A camera is a must", text: "The sight of hundreds of colourful sails against the blue sky makes for incredible photos." }],
    tips: [{ titlu: "Best time to go", text: "If you want to explore the rocky island at the end of the beach, go for a walk in the morning. In years when the tide doesn't cover the sand strip, you can walk straight across to the island and climb up to the old lighthouse at the top, which offers a stunning panorama over the \"kiss of the two seas\"." }],
  },
};
